// P3.10 / PS15.5–15.8, PS11.1 and the P3.8 judge's hole deltas: an 80 × 50 × 20 plate with two
// sketch points on its top and a 40 × 50 × 30 block beside it (values asserted in
// `cadrs_core/tests/part_studio_options.rs`: `hole_start_from_selected_plane_and_up_to_entity`,
// `warnings_for_what_didnt_take`; the tables and callouts in `cadrs_core::hole` tests).
// 01 the tapped hole (PS27.8): Tapped, Tap type Straight tap, M10, Pitch "1.50 mm (Coarse)",
//    Fastener fit None, Thread class 6H (its ">" chevron, P3.11), tap drill Ø8.5, Blind 20 with the 118° point, tapped
//    depth 10.02 and the tap clearance 6.653 threads ((20 − 10.02) / 1.5); the title (and the
//    name) uses the hole depth: "M10x1.50 - 6H ↧ 20 mm". The Merge scope defaults to the part
//    the first hole drills (Part 1).
// 02 the Pitch list: "1.50 mm (Coarse)", "1.25 mm (Fine)", "1.00 mm (Fine)".
// 03 PS15.8 a Drilled Ø5 blind hole with a Diameter tolerance (Deviation +0.10/−0.05) and a
//    Depth tolerance (Max) in the callout: "Ø 5 mm +0.10/−0.05 ↧ 10 mm MAX".
// 04 PS15.6 a Ø9.75 × 12 counterbore over a Ø5 × 20, started from the selected plane (the
//    block's top, 10 above the plate): the counterbore ends 2 below the plate's top (10 of its 12
//    in the air), where Start from part would cut it 12 deep.
// 04a P3.11 (PS15.8) the counterbore's tolerances: Counterbore Ø tolerance Deviation +0.20/−0
//    and Counterbore depth tolerance Symmetrical ±0.10, each section's rows indented under its
//    checkbox: "Ø 5 mm ↧ 20 mm | ⌴Ø 9.75 mm +0.20/−0.00 ↧ 12 mm ±0.10".
// 04b the Countersink tab with a Countersink angle tolerance (±1.0°, degrees):
//    "Ø 5 mm ↧ 20 mm | ⌵Ø 11.2 mm X 90° ±1.0" (the title cut with "…"); started from the part
//    again (fix round 1: from the block's top the 3.1 mm deep cone was all in the air), so the
//    countersinks' cones show in the plate's top.
// 05 PS15.7 Up to entity, the Top plane (the plate's bottom), with an Offset of 5: the full
//    diameter stops 5 short of it; the Offset's distance inline on its checkbox row, with its
//    flip, as the extrude's Offset distance (P3.11).
// 06 PS15.5 the PEM® type: a CLS-M4 self-clinching nut's Ø5.41 +0.08/−0 mounting hole
//    (PennEngineering's table), Through all.
// 07 PS11.1 accepted with a third point between the plate and the block (over no part in the
//    Merge scope): the hole builds with a warning, its row amber with the warning glyph and the
//    reason on hover ("1 hole doesn't reach a part in the merge scope").
